  "type": "multiple-choice",
  "originalQuery": "You are tasked with setting up a relational database that supports the PostgreSQL engine on Google Cloud. The database must be highly available and capable of automatic failover without data loss in case of a zone outage. Which configuration should you choose?",
  "originalOptions": "A. Set up a Cloud Spanner instance with a multi-region configuration for high availability.<br/>B. Use Cloud SQL for PostgreSQL with a single zone instance and scheduled backups.<br/>C. Deploy a self-managed PostgreSQL cluster on Compute Engine VMs with manual failover across zones.<br/>D. Configure Cloud SQL for PostgreSQL with a regional instance and synchronous replication.",
  "domain": "Deploy scalable and highly available databases in Google Cloud",
